"""Blocks of one PS/2 port (keyboard or mouse): the receiver, the host-to-device transmitter, and the register file in the format of the Altera University Program PS/2
controller (the Linux driver altera_ps2, DT compatible "altr,ps2-1.0": DATA at +0, CONTROL at +4). Generated by BARG against hand-written golden models
(golden/<name>.py), never shown to the generator. The lines are open drain: the block drives a line low or releases it; the testbench (or the pin) pulls it high."""
from __future__ import annotations

import sys
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).parent.parent / "gpu-soc"))
from build_gpu_soc import block, i, o, port  # noqa: E402

W = 32
CLK = port("p_clk", "clk", "in", 1, "clock")
RST = port("p_rst", "rst", "in", 1, "reset")

PS2_RX = block("b_ps2_rx", "ps2_rx", """
    The receiver of a PS/2 port. clk_i and dat_i (1 bit each) are the two lines. Held state: c1, c2, c3 (the clock line passed through three flip-flops), d1, d2 (the data line
    through two), all 1 at reset; cnt (4 bits, the bits received so far in the frame), sh (11 bits, the bits received, the first in bit 0), idle (16 bits, cycles since the last
    falling edge, saturating at 65535), and valid (1 bit), dout (8 bits) and perr (1 bit), all 0 at reset. On each rising clock edge, after reset: c1 becomes clk_i, c2 becomes c1,
    c3 becomes c2, d1 becomes dat_i, d2 becomes d1 (the values held before the edge); valid and perr become 0 unless set below. fall is 1 when c3 is 1 and c2 is 0 (a falling edge of the clock
    line). When fall is 1: idle becomes 0; bit cnt of sh becomes d2; and when cnt is 10 (this was the last bit of the frame) cnt becomes 0 and: if bit 0 of sh is 0 (start), d2 is 1 (stop) and the XOR of bits
    9 down to 1 of sh is 1 (odd parity over the 8 data bits and the parity bit), valid becomes 1 and dout becomes bits 8:1 of sh; otherwise perr becomes 1; when cnt is not 10, cnt becomes cnt plus 1.
    When fall is 0: idle becomes idle plus 1 unless it is 65535; and when idle is 32767 (before the edge) cnt becomes 0 (a frame that stalled is dropped). The outputs valid, dout and perr show the held values.
""", [CLK, RST, i("clk_i", 1, "control"), i("dat_i", 1, "control"), o("valid", 1, "control"), o("dout", 8, "data"), o("perr", 1, "control")], reset="sync", latency=1)

PS2_TX = block("b_ps2_tx", "ps2_tx", """
    The host-to-device transmitter of a PS/2 port. clk_i and dat_i (1 bit each) are the two lines, start (1 bit) starts a transmission of data (8 bits) when the transmitter is idle. Held state, all 0 at reset
    except as said: c1, c2, c3, d1, d2 (the lines through flip-flops as in a receiver: 1 at reset), st (2 bits: 0 idle, 1 inhibit, 2 sending), hold (14 bits), n (4 bits, falling clock edges seen since the request), sh (9 bits: the 8
    data bits, bit 0 first, then the odd parity bit, which is 1 when the data has an even number of ones), done (1 bit) and err (1 bit). On each rising clock edge, after reset: c1 becomes clk_i, c2 becomes c1, c3 becomes
    c2, d1 becomes dat_i, d2 becomes d1; done becomes 0 unless set below. fall is 1 when c3 is 1 and c2 is 0 and rise is 1 when c3 is 0 and c2 is 1. State 0: when start is 1, sh becomes data followed by its parity bit, hold becomes 0, err becomes 0 and st becomes 1.
    State 1 (inhibit): hold becomes hold plus 1, and when hold is 16383 st becomes 2 and n becomes 0. State 2: when fall is 1, n becomes n plus 1 (n counts up to 12); when n is 12 and rise is 1: done becomes 1, err becomes d2 (1 when the device did not
    acknowledge by pulling the data line low) and st becomes 0. Outputs, combinational from the held state: clk_low is 1 in state 1 (the clock line is held low) and 0 otherwise; dat_low is 1 in state 2 when n is 0 or 1 (the start bit),
    or when n is from 2 to 10 and bit n minus 2 of sh is 0 (a 0 bit is sent by holding the line low); and 0 otherwise; busy is 1 when st is not 0; done and err show the held values.
""", [CLK, RST, i("clk_i", 1, "control"), i("dat_i", 1, "control"), i("start", 1, "control"), i("data", 8, "data"), o("clk_low", 1, "control"), o("dat_low", 1, "control"),
      o("busy", 1, "control"), o("done", 1, "control"), o("err", 1, "control")], reset="sync", latency=1)

PS2_REGS = block("b_ps2_regs", "ps2_regs", """
    The registers of a PS/2 port, in the format of the Altera University Program PS/2 controller. Held state, all 0 at reset: a receive FIFO kept as eight 8-bit registers fifo0 to fifo7 (every one reset to 0; fifo0 is the oldest byte, and when the oldest byte leaves, fifo<k> becomes fifo<k+1> for k from 0 to 6 and fifo7 becomes 0) with count cnt (4 bits, how many of them hold a byte), re (1 bit,
    read interrupt enable) and ce (1 bit, command error). Inputs from the receiver: rx_valid (a byte rx_byte, 8 bits, has arrived) and from the transmitter: tx_busy, tx_done and tx_err. we is 1 for a store and re_pulse is 1 for a
    load, to the register chosen by bit 2 of addr (0 DATA, 1 CONTROL); wdata is the word stored. avail is cnt. On each rising clock edge, after reset: when re_pulse is 1 and bit 2 of addr is 0 and avail is not 0, the oldest byte
    leaves the FIFO (cnt goes down by 1); when rx_valid is 1 and the FIFO is not full (counting a byte that leaves in the same cycle as one less), rx_byte joins it (cnt goes up by 1) and the bytes stay in arrival order; when we is
    1 and bit 2 of addr is 1, re becomes bit 0 of wdata and ce becomes 0; when tx_done is 1 and tx_err is 1, ce becomes 1. tx_start is 1 when we is 1, bit 2 of addr is 0 and tx_busy is 0, and 0 otherwise; tx_data is always bits 7:0 of wdata (whether or not tx_start is 1). rdata (32 bits, combinational on addr and the held state): for bit 2 of addr 0: bits 31:16 are avail, bit 15 is 1 when avail is not 0, and bits 7:0 are fifo0 (the oldest byte; 0 when avail is 0, never an unset value), the other bits 0; for bit 2 of addr 1:
    bit 0 is re, bit 8 is 1 when re is 1 and avail is not 0 (read interrupt pending), bit 10 is ce, the other bits 0. irq is 1 when re is 1 and avail is not 0.
""", [CLK, RST, i("we", 1, "control"), i("re_pulse", 1, "control"), i("addr", W, "addr"), i("wdata", W, "data"), i("rx_valid", 1, "control"), i("rx_byte", 8, "data"),
      i("tx_busy", 1, "control"), i("tx_done", 1, "control"), i("tx_err", 1, "control"), o("rdata", W, "data"), o("tx_start", 1, "control"), o("tx_data", 8, "data"), o("irq", 1, "control")],
      reset="sync", latency=1)

PS2_FIFO = block("b_ps2_fifo", "ps2_fifo", """
    A first-in first-out queue of eight bytes. Held state, all 0 at reset: eight 8-bit registers q0 to q7 (q0 is the oldest byte) and the count cnt (4 bits, how many of them hold a byte). On each rising clock edge, after reset:
    when pop is 1 and cnt is not 0, the oldest byte leaves (q<k> becomes q<k+1> for k from 0 to 6, q7 becomes 0, and cnt goes down by 1); when push is 1 and the queue is not full (a byte that leaves in the same cycle counts as one
    free place), din joins it as the newest byte, after the bytes that were already there, and cnt goes up by 1. If both happen in one cycle, the pop is done first and then the push. When the queue is full and nothing leaves, push is ignored.
    head is q0 (combinational, 0 when cnt is 0) and count is cnt (4 bits, combinational).
""", [CLK, RST, i("pop", 1, "control"), i("push", 1, "control"), i("din", 8, "data"), o("head", 8, "data"), o("count", 4, "data")], reset="sync", latency=1)

PS2_CTL = block("b_ps2_ctl", "ps2_ctl", """
    The registers of a PS/2 port, in the format of the Altera University Program PS/2 controller, around a receive queue that is a separate block: head (8 bits, the oldest received byte, 0 when the queue is empty) and count
    (4 bits, how many bytes wait) are inputs. Held state, all 0 at reset: re (1 bit, read interrupt enable) and ce (1 bit, command error). Other inputs: tx_busy, tx_done and tx_err from the transmitter; we is 1 for a store and
    re_pulse is 1 for a load, to the register chosen by bit 2 of addr (0 DATA, 1 CONTROL); wdata is the word stored. pop is 1 when re_pulse is 1 and bit 2 of addr is 0 (combinational). On each rising clock edge, after reset:
    when we is 1 and bit 2 of addr is 1, re becomes bit 0 of wdata and ce becomes 0; when tx_done is 1 and tx_err is 1, ce becomes 1. tx_start is 1 when we is 1, bit 2 of addr is 0 and tx_busy is 0, and 0 otherwise; tx_data
    is always bits 7:0 of wdata. rdata (32 bits, combinational): for bit 2 of addr 0: bits 31:16 are count, bit 15 is 1 when count is not 0, bits 7:0 are head, the other bits 0; for bit 2 of addr 1: bit 0 is re, bit 8 is 1
    when re is 1 and count is not 0, bit 10 is ce, the other bits 0. irq is 1 when re is 1 and count is not 0.
""", [CLK, RST, i("we", 1, "control"), i("re_pulse", 1, "control"), i("addr", W, "addr"), i("wdata", W, "data"), i("head", 8, "data"), i("count", 4, "data"),
      i("tx_busy", 1, "control"), i("tx_done", 1, "control"), i("tx_err", 1, "control"), o("rdata", W, "data"), o("pop", 1, "control"), o("tx_start", 1, "control"), o("tx_data", 8, "data"), o("irq", 1, "control")],
      reset="sync", latency=1)

BLOCKS = [PS2_RX, PS2_TX, PS2_REGS, PS2_FIFO, PS2_CTL]
